 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Something classic and simple like Cha Cha Slide or Uptown Funk would be good. Keep the steps basic and everyone can join in. Then ask the music guy to keep it simple and play it after the band has wound down. People love line dance when it' not too cheesy. Which one? There are several Cha Cha Slides. The one with the simple cha cha steps is the one you' looking for. Not necessarily. A good live band is worth the price. Roughly ten dollars an hour, including a couple of instruments and a DJ. Think of it as a night out rather than a lessons. Then keep it simple and look for simple classic. Cha Cha Slide I recommend works.",
